# ==============================================================================
# KEERTI COUTURE — ROOT REPOSITORY ENVIRONMENT OVERVIEW (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
#
# Keerti Couture is structured as a full-stack monorepo:
# - backend/  : Node.js / Express / MongoDB Atelier API
# - frontend/ : Next.js 16 / React 19 / Tailwind CSS Luxury E-Commerce Portal
#
# For local development or deployment, configure environment variables in each
# corresponding workspace directory:
#
# 1. BACKEND CONFIGURATION:
#    Copy backend/.env.example to backend/.env
#    Key variables include:
#      - PORT=5000
#      - NODE_ENV=development
#      - MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/tailor_shop
#      - JWT_SECRET=your_32_character_cryptographic_secret
#      - ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001
#      - CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
#      - SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, FROM_EMAIL
#      - RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET (Optional for portfolio demo)
#
# 2. FRONTEND CONFIGURATION:
#    Copy frontend/.env.example to frontend/.env.local
#    Key variables include:
#      - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
#
# 3. DOCKER COMPOSE CONFIGURATION:
#    If running via docker-compose, root environment variables or docker-compose.yml
#    will inject these settings into containerized backend and frontend services.
#
# NEVER COMMIT ACTUAL .ENV OR .ENV.LOCAL FILES WITH SECRETS TO REPOSITORY.
# ==============================================================================

